                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2610.24791/2610.24791v1/arch_main1.png",
                "caption": "Figure 3:Illustration of the UniAVC framework. (a) Two transformer stacks process video and audio, intersecting exclusively at per-block cross-attention bridges whose modulation is driven by the partner branch’s noise level. Reference latents enter as in-context tokens concatenated to target tokens, with attention masks applied so that reference tokens do not attend to noisy tokens in either self- or cross-attention blocks. (b) Each branch first attains full generative and editing competence on unimodal data in parallel; both branches are subsequently frozen, and the paired corpus is used solely to train the cross-modal bridges.",
